			"notes": "CHANGELOG - Vision Goggles v0.1.2-Alpha\n\nNew Features\n*   Modular Goggles: Added a new type of goggles that allows dynamic installation of up to 2 different vision modules.\n*   Hydro Goggles: Fully implemented goggles for underwater vision with custom textures and dedicated crafting recipe.\n*   Biometric Scanner Goggles: Fully implemented goggles for entity health and distance scanning with custom textures and dedicated crafting recipe.\n*   Modification Station: New functional block with a custom user interface (GUI) to install modules onto goggles.\n*   New Item - Electrical Parts: Added as the fundamental component for crafting modules and advanced electronics.\n*   Battery Expansion Module: Increases the total energy capacity of modular goggles by 50% (x1.5).\n*   Vision Modules: Added NVG, Thermal, Hydro, and Biometric modules as individual items for the modification system.\n\nProgression and Crafting\n*   Complex Crafting System: Redesigned all recipes to follow a logical progression using Netherite, Gold, Amethyst, Nether Stars, and Electrical Parts.\n*   Sequential Upgrading: Thermal Goggles now require a pair of Night Vision Goggles as a base component.\n*   New Base Recipe: Added a recipe for Electrical Parts using Redstone, Copper, and Iron.\n*   Proportional Recharging: Batteries now recharge 50% of the current maximum capacity, correctly supporting goggles with expansion modules.\n\nVisual Improvements and Rendering\n*   Thermal Vision Optimization: Switched detection color to Cyan to eliminate false positives from sand and warm-colored blocks.\n*   Silhouette Refinement: Adjusted scale (1.10x) and vertical centering to ensure heat silhouettes fit entity models and armor perfectly.\n*   Item Models: Added proper 2D models and textures for all new goggles, modules, and components.\n*   Custom GUI: Cleaned up the modification station interface by hiding default titles to focus on the custom texture design.\n\nFixes and Adjustments (Server Stability)\n*   Forge Server Fix: Isolated client-only rendering classes (RenderLayer) to prevent NoClassDefFoundError on dedicated servers.\n*   Cloth Config Isolation: Refactored configuration logic to separate GUI creation from data handling, preventing crashes on servers where Cloth Config is not present.\n*   Dynamic Battery Logic: Fixed an issue where the system did not recognize capacity increases beyond the base 6,000 ticks during recharging.\n*   HUD Correction: The battery percentage display now correctly calculates the 100% mark based on the dynamic maximum capacity (including expansions).\n*   Slot Compatibility: Restricted goggles to face, eyes, and eyewear slots only (removed compatibility with the head/helmet slot in Curios and Accessories).\n*   Code Cleanup: Removed redundant duplicated shader folder structure.\n\nLocalization\n*   Complete translations for all items, blocks, keybinds, and tooltips in: English (US/GB), Spanish (ES, MX, AR, CL), German, French, Italian, Portuguese, Polish, and Russian."
		},
